10:[["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"relative overflow-hidden border-b border-border bg-[#eef3f8] py-16 text-slate-900 sm:py-24","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute inset-0 opacity-70 [background-image:radial-gradient(circle_at_88%_12%,rgba(14,116,144,0.12),transparent_32%),radial-gradient(circle_at_10%_80%,rgba(37,99,235,0.10),transparent_36%)]"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"container-site relative","children":[["$","$L1a",null,{"href":"/highlights/blogs","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-teal-700 hover:text-teal-800","children":[["$","$L1b",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7","key":"1l729n"}],["path",{"d":"M19 12H5","key":"x3x0zl"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left size-4"}],"All articles"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 max-w-4xl","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full border px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold transition-colors border-transparent bg-secondary/10 text-secondary dark:text-blue-300","children":"NEP 2020"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-5 font-heading text-4xl leading-tight font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl","children":"Overview of the National Education Policy"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-600","children":"On 29th July 2020, PM Narendra Modi’s government approved the National Education Policy (NEP 2020). The policy brings an extensive range of reforms aimed at transforming the Indian education ecosystem. It is looked…"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-5 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-500","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"CITIS InfoTech Editorial"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5","children":[["$","$L1b",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M8 2v3","key":"1ioesn"}],["path",{"d":"M16 2v3","key":"otl347"}],["rect",{"x":"3","y":"3","width":"18","height":"18","rx":"2","key":"h1oib"}],["path",{"d":"M3 9h18","key":"1pudct"}],["path",{"d":"M8 13h.01","key":"1sbv64"}],["path",{"d":"M12 13h.01","key":"y0uutt"}],["path",{"d":"M16 13h.01","key":"wip0gl"}],["path",{"d":"M8 17h.01","key":"p3bg7i"}],["path",{"d":"M12 17h.01","key":"p32p05"}],["path",{"d":"M16 17h.01","key":"ql8jdd"}]],"className":"lucide-calendar-days size-4"}],"27 January 2022"]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5","children":[["$","$L1b",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["circle",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10","key":"1mglay"}],["path",{"d":"M12 6v6l4 2","key":"mmk7yg"}]],"className":"lucide-clock size-4"}],"10 min read"]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-[#e8edf5] dark:bg-slate-900","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-site grid gap-10 py-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_13rem] lg:gap-16 lg:py-20","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl","children":[[["$","section","Overview",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Overview"}],[["$","p","On 29th July 2020, PM Narendra Modi’s government approved the National Education Policy (NEP 2020). The policy brings an extensive range of reforms aimed at transforming the Indian education ecosystem. It is looked upon as a focused decision that introduces several new initiatives, subjects, learning methods, teaching techniques, etc. NEP 2020 is more closely aligned with the existing and futuristic skills needs of the country and aims at helping to strengthen the skills of the Indian youth in subject matters slated to be the world’s future.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"On 29th July 2020, PM Narendra Modi’s government approved the National Education Policy (NEP 2020). The policy brings an extensive range of reforms aimed at transforming the Indian education ecosystem. It is looked upon as a focused decision that introduces several new initiatives, subjects, learning methods, teaching techniques, etc. NEP 2020 is more closely aligned with the existing and futuristic skills needs of the country and aims at helping to strengthen the skills of the Indian youth in subject matters slated to be the world’s future."}],"$L1c"]]}],"$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e"],"$L2f"]}],"$L30"]}]}]]}],"$L31","$L32"]
1c:["$","p","The NEP 2020 is a 66-page long document which you can read on the link https://www.mhrd.gov.in/sites/upload_files/mhrd/files/NEP_Final_English_0.pdf. This blog highlights the key takeaways of NEP 2020 to get a quick insight into what kind of changes and reforms will NEP 2020 bring to the Indian education system.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The NEP 2020 is a 66-page long document which you can read on the link https://www.mhrd.gov.in/sites/upload_files/mhrd/files/NEP_Final_English_0.pdf. This blog highlights the key takeaways of NEP 2020 to get a quick insight into what kind of changes and reforms will NEP 2020 bring to the Indian education system."}]
1d:["$","section","What is the Vision of the National Education Policy?",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"What is the Vision of the National Education Policy?"}],[["$","p","The NEP 2020 is a comprehensive initiative taken by PM Modi’s government. It is a visionary and sustainable decision that envisages a better, more learned, responsible, and more equality-based society that provides equal learning opportunities for everyone throughout the country. Let us glance through NEP 2020’s vision.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The NEP 2020 is a comprehensive initiative taken by PM Modi’s government. It is a visionary and sustainable decision that envisages a better, more learned, responsible, and more equality-based society that provides equal learning opportunities for everyone throughout the country. Let us glance through NEP 2020’s vision."}],["$","p","Develop an education system that contributes to an equitable and vibrant society by providing high-quality education to every citizen of the country.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Develop an education system that contributes to an equitable and vibrant society by providing high-quality education to every citizen of the country."}],["$","p","Develop skills, dispositions, and values that support responsible commitment to human rights, foster sustainable development, global well-being, and excellent living to make Indian youth global citizens.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Develop skills, dispositions, and values that support responsible commitment to human rights, foster sustainable development, global well-being, and excellent living to make Indian youth global citizens."}],["$","p","Develop a sense of respect towards Constitutional values, fundamental rights, responsibilities, and conscious awareness about one’s role in the ever-changing world. Develop patriotism, bonding with the country, help and educate people to become more responsible citizens of a progressive nation.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Develop a sense of respect towards Constitutional values, fundamental rights, responsibilities, and conscious awareness about one’s role in the ever-changing world. Develop patriotism, bonding with the country, help and educate people to become more responsible citizens of a progressive nation."}]]]}]
1e:["$","section","What are the Key Changes brought through the NEP 2020?",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"What are the Key Changes brought through the NEP 2020?"}],[["$","p","The National Education Policy 2020 aims to empower everyone with quality education, no matter the person's intellectual level. It also intends to bridge the skill gap between education and the industry’s requirements – something which has been widespread concern with the Indian education system so far. And most importantly, the NEP aims at grooming and training the new generation right from an early age.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The National Education Policy 2020 aims to empower everyone with quality education, no matter the person's intellectual level. It also intends to bridge the skill gap between education and the industry’s requirements – something which has been widespread concern with the Indian education system so far. And most importantly, the NEP aims at grooming and training the new generation right from an early age."}],["$","p","Some of the key changes brought by the Indian government through the NEP 2020 include the following.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Some of the key changes brought by the Indian government through the NEP 2020 include the following."}]]]}]
1f:["$","section","School Structure Restructuring",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"School Structure Restructuring"}],[["$","p","While the existing academic structure considers 10 + 2, the new one will replace it with a 5 + 3 + 3 + 4 system. So, the NEP will not increase the number of academic years but only will break it down and restructure it. The new structure is created based on the cognitive-developmental stages, including early childhood, school years, and then the advanced – the secondary stage. Let us look at each of the stages.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"While the existing academic structure considers 10 + 2, the new one will replace it with a 5 + 3 + 3 + 4 system. So, the NEP will not increase the number of academic years but only will break it down and restructure it. The new structure is created based on the cognitive-developmental stages, including early childhood, school years, and then the advanced – the secondary stage. Let us look at each of the stages."}]]]}]
20:["$","section","Stage 1",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Stage 1"}],[["$","p","The first five years are termed the Foundation Stage, and children from the age group of 3 to 8 years will come under this category. It also includes the first three learning years (preschool, playgroup, nursery, and KG). Besides, children from 6 to 8 years (first and second standard) are also included in the same group to keep up with their understanding of fundamental concepts, linguistic development, and activities.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The first five years are termed the Foundation Stage, and children from the age group of 3 to 8 years will come under this category. It also includes the first three learning years (preschool, playgroup, nursery, and KG). Besides, children from 6 to 8 years (first and second standard) are also included in the same group to keep up with their understanding of fundamental concepts, linguistic development, and activities."}]]]}]
21:["$","section","Stage 2",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Stage 2"}],[["$","p","The second stage (three years) is termed the Preparatory Stage. This category will include students from standard third to fifth, and children from age 8 to 11 will be included in it. This stage will focus on cognitive development through classroom activities, interactive sessions, and numeracy skills. Besides, until class 5, students will be allowed to interact with their teacher and vice versa in the mother-tongue or regional language, as per the state.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The second stage (three years) is termed the Preparatory Stage. This category will include students from standard third to fifth, and children from age 8 to 11 will be included in it. This stage will focus on cognitive development through classroom activities, interactive sessions, and numeracy skills. Besides, until class 5, students will be allowed to interact with their teacher and vice versa in the mother-tongue or regional language, as per the state."}]]]}]
22:["$","section","Stage 3",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Stage 3"}],[["$","p","Stage 3 is the middle stage, and it includes students from class six to eight. This stage will involve learning coding to develop critical thinking abilities in the children. Besides, this stage will also promote learning in sciences, experiential learning, arts, and social studies.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Stage 3 is the middle stage, and it includes students from class six to eight. This stage will involve learning coding to develop critical thinking abilities in the children. Besides, this stage will also promote learning in sciences, experiential learning, arts, and social studies."}]]]}]
23:["$","section","Stage 4",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Stage 4"}],[["$","p","Stage 4 constitutes the secondary stage and includes class ninth to twelfth. Since this stage will comprise a multidisciplinary study, it will allow students to choose a combination of various subjects.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Stage 4 constitutes the secondary stage and includes class ninth to twelfth. Since this stage will comprise a multidisciplinary study, it will allow students to choose a combination of various subjects."}],["$","p","A multidisciplinary approach will Eliminate the Rigid Separation Between Streams.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"A multidisciplinary approach will Eliminate the Rigid Separation Between Streams."}],["$","p","In India, we often consider people studying engineering and medical sciences to be intellectually better and higher than those pursuing arts or, perhaps, languages. Of course, we’ve been living with this inappropriate approach for years. But, what’s even more critical is that this approach has led us to restrict the career opportunities for students learning unconventional subjects and allowing only the conventional ones to grow!",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"In India, we often consider people studying engineering and medical sciences to be intellectually better and higher than those pursuing arts or, perhaps, languages. Of course, we’ve been living with this inappropriate approach for years. But, what’s even more critical is that this approach has led us to restrict the career opportunities for students learning unconventional subjects and allowing only the conventional ones to grow!"}],["$","p","Nevertheless, the multidisciplinary approach has the potential to revolutionize people’s approach, thought process, and therefore augment the career opportunities for those choosing unconventional subjects. So, what will the multidisciplinary approach do? It eliminates the rigid separation between streams, and therefore,",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Nevertheless, the multidisciplinary approach has the potential to revolutionize people’s approach, thought process, and therefore augment the career opportunities for those choosing unconventional subjects. So, what will the multidisciplinary approach do? It eliminates the rigid separation between streams, and therefore,"}],["$","p","Arts, Commerce, and science will be brought at an equal pace, thus eliminating the distinction that was being made based on the subjects chosen throughout.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Arts, Commerce, and science will be brought at an equal pace, thus eliminating the distinction that was being made based on the subjects chosen throughout."}],["$","p","Students will be allowed to study diverse subjects. For instance, if someone learning French wants to study Physics, they will be allowed to do so.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Students will be allowed to study diverse subjects. For instance, if someone learning French wants to study Physics, they will be allowed to do so."}],"$L33"]]}]
24:["$","section","Board Exams will have their Approach, Objectives, and Face Changed!",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Board Exams will have their Approach, Objectives, and Face Changed!"}],[["$","p","For years, we’ve been living with the fears of board exams. Of course, they’ve always been a significant step to qualify for the next level of education; but practically, board exams aren’t any different from the other examinations we’ve attended so far.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"For years, we’ve been living with the fears of board exams. Of course, they’ve always been a significant step to qualify for the next level of education; but practically, board exams aren’t any different from the other examinations we’ve attended so far."}],["$","p","The NEP 2020 has brought a number of reforms to eliminate the fear of board examinations by making a lot of changes to them, one of which is that they will be made easier! Let us take a look at some other changes pertaining to board examinations of the NEP 2020.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The NEP 2020 has brought a number of reforms to eliminate the fear of board examinations by making a lot of changes to them, one of which is that they will be made easier! Let us take a look at some other changes pertaining to board examinations of the NEP 2020."}]]]}]
25:["$","section","Subjects will have two levels of difficulty – standard and higher",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Subjects will have two levels of difficulty – standard and higher"}],[["$","p","NCERT has been given the responsibility to prepare guidelines in consultation with The State Council of Educational Research and Training (SCERTs), and Boards of Assessment (BoAs), and PARAKH. Besides, teachers will have to prepare themselves for a transformation in the assessment system.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"NCERT has been given the responsibility to prepare guidelines in consultation with The State Council of Educational Research and Training (SCERTs), and Boards of Assessment (BoAs), and PARAKH. Besides, teachers will have to prepare themselves for a transformation in the assessment system."}],["$","p","Mandatory Vocational Studies should be made a part of the syllabus.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Mandatory Vocational Studies should be made a part of the syllabus."}],["$","p","The Indian education system, so far, focused more on completing the syllabus rather than imparting practical value. Making vocational study compulsory is projected to bridge the gap between industry needs and education. In this view, NEP 2020 has made vocational studies mandatory and a part of the syllabus. Some of the benefits of this initiative include the following.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The Indian education system, so far, focused more on completing the syllabus rather than imparting practical value. Making vocational study compulsory is projected to bridge the gap between industry needs and education. In this view, NEP 2020 has made vocational studies mandatory and a part of the syllabus. Some of the benefits of this initiative include the following."}]]]}]
26:["$","section","Leveraging Multilingualism to Promote Cultural Values",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Leveraging Multilingualism to Promote Cultural Values"}],[["$","p","NEP 2020 does not just aim at creating a modern globalized generation, but citizens that love their country and have a deep-rooted pride in being an Indian. One of the ways to do it is by promoting Indian languages in the syllabus. In this view, the NEP 2020 comprises the following changes.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"NEP 2020 does not just aim at creating a modern globalized generation, but citizens that love their country and have a deep-rooted pride in being an Indian. One of the ways to do it is by promoting Indian languages in the syllabus. In this view, the NEP 2020 comprises the following changes."}],["$","p","Until the 5th grade, the medium of education will remain the home language or the mother tongue or the locally spoken language",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Until the 5th grade, the medium of education will remain the home language or the mother tongue or the locally spoken language"}],["$","p","The respective state or Union Territory will decide the three languages to be taught to the students",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The respective state or Union Territory will decide the three languages to be taught to the students"}]]]}]
27:["$","section","Students will have all classical languages as an option",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Students will have all classical languages as an option"}],[["$","p","As one of the language formulae, Sanskrit will be given more value and importance in secondary and higher education",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"As one of the language formulae, Sanskrit will be given more value and importance in secondary and higher education"}]]]}]
28:["$","section","Adoption of Comprehensive Education and Introduction of Holistic Report Cards",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Adoption of Comprehensive Education and Introduction of Holistic Report Cards"}],[["$","p","States and Union Territories will have to design a comprehensive report card that will include the score for theoretical subjects, and at the same time, also include credit points for taking part in extra or co-curricular activities. Besides, the report or progress card will also include the assessment of self, peers, and teachers.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"States and Union Territories will have to design a comprehensive report card that will include the score for theoretical subjects, and at the same time, also include credit points for taking part in extra or co-curricular activities. Besides, the report or progress card will also include the assessment of self, peers, and teachers."}],["$","p","These report cards are projected to help students realize and assess their potential and progress across cognitive, psychomotor, and socio-emotional skills. Aside from that, the progress card will also include participation in various sports, drama, quizzes, debates, and other group activities. These changes will help improve the teacher-student relationship and even foster parents’ involvement in the child’s progress.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"These report cards are projected to help students realize and assess their potential and progress across cognitive, psychomotor, and socio-emotional skills. Aside from that, the progress card will also include participation in various sports, drama, quizzes, debates, and other group activities. These changes will help improve the teacher-student relationship and even foster parents’ involvement in the child’s progress."}],["$","p","Apart from the above, proper software will have to be developed and implemented across the educational ecosystem to maintain the child’s scores, along with the entire academic record to help him make an informed career choice when he or she grows up.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Apart from the above, proper software will have to be developed and implemented across the educational ecosystem to maintain the child’s scores, along with the entire academic record to help him make an informed career choice when he or she grows up."}]]]}]
29:["$","section","Setting up Foreign University Campus in India",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Setting up Foreign University Campus in India"}],[["$","p","As per the NEP 2020, around 100 foreign colleges will be allowed to open their branches across India. Besides, Indian SAT will be conducted, and a lot of undergraduate institutions will be given autonomy in their financial and administrative matters based on the accreditation they’ve got.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"As per the NEP 2020, around 100 foreign colleges will be allowed to open their branches across India. Besides, Indian SAT will be conducted, and a lot of undergraduate institutions will be given autonomy in their financial and administrative matters based on the accreditation they’ve got."}]]]}]
2a:["$","section","Single Regulatory Body",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Single Regulatory Body"}],[["$","p","Under this, the NEP 2020 comprises the following changes.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Under this, the NEP 2020 comprises the following changes."}]]]}]
2b:["$","section","The HRD ministry will be termed Education Ministry",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"The HRD ministry will be termed Education Ministry"}],[["$","p","NTA will conduct one common entrance test for all the higher education institutes. The test will be optional and would be conducted twice a year.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"NTA will conduct one common entrance test for all the higher education institutes. The test will be optional and would be conducted twice a year."}],["$","p","UGC and AICTE will merge to form a single regulatory body called the Higher Education Commission of India (HECI).",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"UGC and AICTE will merge to form a single regulatory body called the Higher Education Commission of India (HECI)."}]]]}]
2c:["$","section","Plans in the Pipeline",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Plans in the Pipeline"}],[["$","p","Include undergraduate programs of three and four years and postgraduate programs of one and two years",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Include undergraduate programs of three and four years and postgraduate programs of one and two years"}],["$","p","MPhil course will be discontinued as a course.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"MPhil course will be discontinued as a course."}],["$","p","Institutions such as IIT will be asked to become more holistic and introduce more courses on humanities and arts.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Institutions such as IIT will be asked to become more holistic and introduce more courses on humanities and arts."}]]]}]
2d:["$","section","Optimization of School Space",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Optimization of School Space"}],[["$","p","Making optimal use of school space to enable comprehensive learning and awareness is critical from the viewpoint of the holistic development of children. In this view, the NEP 2020 brings the following reforms to make efficient utilization of school space.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Making optimal use of school space to enable comprehensive learning and awareness is critical from the viewpoint of the holistic development of children. In this view, the NEP 2020 brings the following reforms to make efficient utilization of school space."}],["$","p","Use school space beyond school hours and public library for ICT-equipped adult education courses",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Use school space beyond school hours and public library for ICT-equipped adult education courses"}],["$","p","Build free boarding facilities matching the class of Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas, especially for students from socio-economically unprivileged backgrounds.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Build free boarding facilities matching the class of Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas, especially for students from socio-economically unprivileged backgrounds."}],["$","p","Include sampling of vocational craft such as metalwork, electronic work, carpentry, etc., from class six to eight.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Include sampling of vocational craft such as metalwork, electronic work, carpentry, etc., from class six to eight."}],["$","p","Another important initiative is that of the establishment of an autonomous body called the National Education Technology Forum (NETF). NETF will facilitate a platform to foster the exchange of views, understand the use of technology to improve learning, plan assessments, etc., for schools as well as colleges.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Another important initiative is that of the establishment of an autonomous body called the National Education Technology Forum (NETF). NETF will facilitate a platform to foster the exchange of views, understand the use of technology to improve learning, plan assessments, etc., for schools as well as colleges."}],["$","p","Besides, the NETF will continually analyze and categorize emerging technologies within the education sector, depending on their potential. The forum will also present their inputs to the education ministry, after which the ministry will officially identify those technologies. However, the emergence of these technologies will be subject to responses from the education ecosystem.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"Besides, the NETF will continually analyze and categorize emerging technologies within the education sector, depending on their potential. The forum will also present their inputs to the education ministry, after which the ministry will officially identify those technologies. However, the emergence of these technologies will be subject to responses from the education ecosystem."}]]]}]
2e:["$","section","Conclusion",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl","children":"Conclusion"}],[["$","p","NEP 2020, with the reforms it intends to bring, is undoubtedly projected to revolutionize the Indian education ecosystem that was due for changes and improvements for a very long time. Nevertheless, NEP 2020 will achieve its objectives and meet success only if the entire education ecosystem aligns itself with it, and the animators, educators, and the policy-makers work in unison, implement the said policies, and strive for the betterment of the Indian education system and create a brighter generation, capable of making a difference.",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"NEP 2020, with the reforms it intends to bring, is undoubtedly projected to revolutionize the Indian education ecosystem that was due for changes and improvements for a very long time. Nevertheless, NEP 2020 will achieve its objectives and meet success only if the entire education ecosystem aligns itself with it, and the animators, educators, and the policy-makers work in unison, implement the said policies, and strive for the betterment of the Indian education system and create a brighter generation, capable of making a difference."}]]]}]
2f:["$","aside",null,{"className":"mt-12 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-accent bg-primary/5 p-7","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-heading text-xl font-semibold","children":"The practical takeaway"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-7 text-muted-foreground","children":"Start with one meaningful learner outcome, create an authentic way to observe it, and support educators to improve the experience together."}]]}]
